  "summary": "wormgpt-cli ships a remote-access implant with credential/clipboard stealers and HTTP C2",
  "details": "The package ships an implant module (src/implant/implant.js) that spawns bash and powershell child processes and includes a screen-capture helper. A clipboard stealer (src/implant/stealers/clipboard.js) uses execSync with powershell to read the host clipboard. src/protocol.js and src/tui/app.js read host identity via os.homedir() and process.env, load fs/http/https, and issue POST requests carrying hostname and identifier fields, forming a client/operator channel over HTTP. The package name and structure (wormgpt-cli, an 'implant' directory with 'stealers') describe a remote-access trojan / operator tool: installing or loading it introduces implant code, shell-execution primitives, credential/clipboard/screen capture, and HTTP command-and-control on the host.",
